  "prompt": "Return every distinct triple of values [a, b, c] from different positions of nums with a + b + c == 0. Each triple should appear once. Order of triples and order inside a triple do not matter.\n\nSignature:\n    def three_sum(nums: list[int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n\nExamples:\n    three_sum([-1, 0, 1, 2, -1, -4]) -> [[-1, -1, 2], [-1, 0, 1]]",
  "starter": "def three_sum(nums: list[int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    # Your code here\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "def three_sum(nums):\n    nums = sorted(nums)\n    out = []\n    for i in range(len(nums) - 2):\n        if i and nums[i] == nums[i - 1]:\n            continue\n        lo, hi = i + 1, len(nums) - 1\n        while lo < hi:\n            s = nums[i] + nums[lo] + nums[hi]\n            if s < 0:\n                lo += 1\n            elif s > 0:\n                hi -= 1\n            else:\n                out.append([nums[i], nums[lo], nums[hi]])\n                lo += 1\n                while lo < hi and nums[lo] == nums[lo - 1]:\n                    lo += 1\n    return out\n",
