  "prompt": "There are n courses, 0 to n - 1. Each pair [a, b] in prereqs means you must take b before a. Return True if you can take every course (that is, the requirements have no cycle).\n\nSignature:\n    def can_finish(n: int, prereqs: list[list[int]]) -> bool:\n\nExamples:\n    can_finish(2, [[1, 0]]) -> True\n    can_finish(2, [[1, 0], [0, 1]]) -> False",
  "starter": "def can_finish(n: int, prereqs: list[list[int]]) -> bool:\n    # Your code here\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "from collections import deque\n\ndef can_finish(n, prereqs):\n    indeg = [0] * n\n    after = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for a, b in prereqs:\n        after[b].append(a)\n        indeg[a] += 1\n    q = deque(i for i in range(n) if indeg[i] == 0)\n    taken = 0\n    while q:\n        x = q.popleft()\n        taken += 1\n        for y in after[x]:\n            indeg[y] -= 1\n            if indeg[y] == 0:\n                q.append(y)\n    return taken == n\n",
