  "prompt": "nums was sorted ascending with distinct values, then rotated at an unknown point (for example [0,1,2,4,5,6,7] became [4,5,6,7,0,1,2]). Return the index of target, or -1, in O(log n).\n\nSignature:\n    def search_rotated(nums: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n\nExamples:\n    search_rotated([4, 5, 6, 7, 0, 1, 2], 0) -> 4\n    search_rotated([4, 5, 6, 7, 0, 1, 2], 3) -> -1",
  "starter": "def search_rotated(nums: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    # Your code here\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "def search_rotated(nums, target):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(nums) - 1\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if nums[mid] == target:\n            return mid\n        if nums[lo] <= nums[mid]:\n            if nums[lo] <= target < nums[mid]:\n                hi = mid - 1\n            else:\n                lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            if nums[mid] < target <= nums[hi]:\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n    return -1\n",
